---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Kicker from "../../components/Kicker.astro";

const lastUpdated = "28 July 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How RAM Advisory Group collects, uses and protects your personal data."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-8">
    <Kicker>Legal</Kicker>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 font-sans text-sm text-silver-grey">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose-content mt-10 space-y-10 font-sans text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-heading-navy">1. Who We Are</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          RAM Advisory Group ("RAM", "we", "us", "our") is a UK boutique corporate investigations,
          intelligence and risk consultancy. This policy explains how we collect, use and protect
          personal data when you visit ramadvisorygroup.co.uk (the "Site") or otherwise interact with us,
          for example by phone, email, or contact form.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@ramadvisorygroup.co.uk" class="text-heading-navy underline">contact@ramadvisorygroup.co.uk</a>
          &middot; 07919 365173
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-heading-navy">2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            <strong>Enquiry data:</strong> name, organisation, email address, phone number and any
            information you provide when you contact us by form, email or phone.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address, browser type, device information and pages
            visited, collected automatically via cookies and similar technologies when you use the Site.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Case-related data:</strong> where you engage RAM for an investigation, due diligence
            or risk engagement, additional personal data may be collected as part of that specific
            instruction, governed by the terms agreed for that engagement.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-heading-navy">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>To respond to enquiries and provide requested information about our services.</li>
          <li>To deliver, manage and communicate about any engagement you instruct us on.</li>
          <li>To maintain and improve the Site, including basic analytics.</li>
          <li>To comply with our legal, regulatory and professional obligations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Our lawful bases for processing are legitimate interests (responding to enquiries, improving the
          Site), contract (delivering an engagement you've instructed), and legal obligation (regulatory
          and record-keeping requirements), as applicable.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-heading-navy">4. Cookies</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The Site uses cookies to operate correctly and, where consented to, to understand how visitors
          use the Site (analytics). A cookie consent banner allows you to accept or decline non-essential
          cookies. You can also control cookies through your browser settings.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-heading-navy">5. Sharing Your Information</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We do not sell your personal data. We may share information with trusted specialist partners
          (for example digital forensics, surveillance or financial investigation specialists) strictly
          where necessary to deliver an engagement, and with service providers who support our IT,
          hosting and communications — each bound by appropriate confidentiality and data protection
          obligations. We may also disclose information where required by law or to protect our legal
          rights.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-heading-navy">6. Data Retention</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We retain personal data only for as long as necessary for the purposes it was collected,
          including to satisfy any legal, accounting, or reporting requirements. Enquiry data not leading
          to an engagement is typically retained for a limited period before deletion.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-heading-navy">7. Your Rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Under UK GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Access the personal data we hold about you.</li>
          <li>Request correction of inaccurate data.</li>
          <li>Request deletion of your data, in certain circumstances.</li>
          <li>Object to or restrict certain processing.</li>
          <li>Request a copy of your data in a portable format.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          To exercise any of these rights, contact us at
          <a href="mailto:contact@ramadvisorygroup.co.uk" class="text-heading-navy underline">contact@ramadvisorygroup.co.uk</a>.
          You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the
          <a href="https://ico.org.uk" class="text-heading-navy underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          RAM Advisory Group is registered with the ICO as a data controller. You can verify our
          registration directly on the public ICO register:
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://ico.org.uk/ESDWebPages/Entry/ZC229712"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-sm border border-hairline bg-pale-accent px-4 py-2 text-heading-navy underline decoration-heading-navy/40 underline-offset-2 hover:bg-hairline/40"
        >
          <svg
            class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.5"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <path d="M12 3.5 19 6.5v5.2c0 4.6-3 8.3-7 9.3-4-1-7-4.7-7-9.3V6.5Z" />
            <path d="m9.3 12.1 1.9 1.9 3.6-3.9" />
          </svg>
          ICO Registration Reference: ZC229712
        </a>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-heading-navy">8. Security</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Given the sensitive nature of our work, we take appropriate technical and organisational
          measures to protect personal data against unauthorised access, loss, or misuse.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-heading-navy">9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may update this policy from time to time. The "last updated" date above reflects the most
          recent revision.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
